Subject: [PATCH] Venetium 0060 (v1.2): no stack-variable initialization in
 codec DSP code

From Venetium v1.2 (github.com/hamed7ir/venetium 92b73dd), patches/0060-dsp-no-stack-var-init.patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 third_party/dav1d/BUILD.gn         | 16 +++++++++++++++
 third_party/libjpeg_turbo/BUILD.gn |  4 ++++
 third_party/libvpx/BUILD.gn        | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 third_party/libwebp/BUILD.gn       | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 72 insertions(+)

diff --git a/third_party/dav1d/BUILD.gn b/third_party/dav1d/BUILD.gn
index d75d82371339abb0583c48a9b1b299ff5581efb4..5e72ebef6d4a8ca26d16bb5799a943dfaa307731 100644
--- a/third_party/dav1d/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/dav1d/BUILD.gn
@@ -167,6 +167,10 @@ source_set("dav1d_headers") {
 }
 
 static_library("dav1d_8bit") {
+  # Venetium 0060: no automatic stack-variable initialization in these DSP
+  # kernels (fixed-size scratch arrays they overwrite in full; the pattern/zero
+  # fill costs a memset per block). Same opt-out as libaom and V8.
+  configs -= [ "//build/config/compiler:default_init_stack_vars" ]
   configs -= [ "//build/config/compiler:chromium_code" ]
   configs += [
     "//build/config/compiler:no_chromium_code",
@@ -189,6 +193,10 @@ static_library("dav1d_8bit") {
 }
 
